cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its data, please cite the tagged release you used
  (see the repository's Releases), not the live dashboard, which changes over time.
type: software
title: "UAM Airspace Dashboard: 3D corridor designer, overlap analysis and example data"
authors:
  - family-names: Carvalho
    given-names: Lucas Orbolato
    affiliation: Instituto Tecnológico de Aeronáutica (ITA)
  - name: SIGMA-Sky Project
version: ridita-2026.4
date-released: "2026-10-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/projetosigmasky/uam_airspace"
url: "https://projetosigmasky.github.io/uam_airspace/"
abstract: >-
  Client-side dashboard for designing urban air mobility corridors and measuring, by volume,
  how much of them lies inside other airspace structures (helicopter and aircraft special
  routes) and empirical airport-flow envelopes derived from Flightradar24 tracks, with the
  scripts that build those layers.
keywords:
  - urban air mobility
  - airspace design
  - corridors
  - overlap analysis
  - Flightradar24
